#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "184d9e09-3335-5617-8989-e5ab08ca04e7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a3ffab8-22b1-5ff6-b581-2df35360fc18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159549} {:answer/id #uuid "e2eb2f4e-7ab5-5535-849b-49596a5e1b1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159550} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b0bd0d-58a5-5da2-a7d3-f2d3defec647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159551} {:answer/id #uuid "28844849-77a7-5df3-890d-de9c0191d526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159552} {:answer/id #uuid "7078d5e7-d2e8-5893-b018-fc36ef965370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159553}] :answer-field/id #uuid "72b97b25-0523-5c03-8564-83a07b086085" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159548}] :question/id #uuid "11a32556-0b83-5605-b76d-705cb2b8ca2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-143460" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid y) = {\\frac{2x}{y^{2}},\\begin{vmatrix}0 < x < y, 0 < y < 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nFind $P(\\frac{1}{4} < X < \\frac{1}{2} \\mid Y = \\frac{5}{8})$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162392 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "184d9e09-3335-5617-8989-e5ab08ca04e7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76dedc47-c082-5f11-bb91-f5c53a5feef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413404} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e703b0-4bd0-5a40-af83-db0c989a5aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413405} {:answer/id #uuid "db303bfa-69cf-5cf1-86a5-b4a2624334a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413408} {:answer/id #uuid "efd7c23f-d7a0-5417-baaf-c56cd1849f93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413410} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf61311-9fef-553a-a566-6bcfee2063e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76dedc47-c082-5f11-bb91-f5c53a5feef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413404} :answer-field/id #uuid "7133b6f3-994d-586b-8bc7-52facdb8edd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413413}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "990850d6-75f9-5e72-98e4-4c732056938a" :question/math-academy-id "q-143461" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}24xy, & \\,0<x<1,0<y<1-x \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFind $P(Y<X\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(Y\\in A\\,|\\,X=x)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x.$ \n\nUsing the formula for the marginal density function for $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1-x}24xy\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =24x{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =24x{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1-x} \\\\  & =12x(1-x)^{2}-0 \\\\  & =12x(x-1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)={\\begin{aligned}12x(x-1)^{2}, & \\,0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nNow, for $0<x<1,0<y<1-x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{24xy}{12x(x-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{(x-1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y}{(x-1)^{2}}, & \\,0<x<1,0<y<1-x \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute our probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<X\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{3}) & =P(Y<\\frac{1}{3}\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x=\\frac{1}{3})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\frac{2y}{{(\\frac{1}{3}-1)}^{2}}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}(\\frac{1}{18}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
